--TEST--
An extension result is tainted when an argument to the call was tainted, with no declaration in the manifest, so it cannot reach a sink — `rule:security/extension-contagion`
--EXTENSION--
ledger
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Shop\Ledger;

tainted string $input = "a line";

// `echoString` returns its argument. A plain argument gives a plain result,
// so `writeLine` accepts it.
Ledger::writeLine(Ledger::echoString("a line"));

// A tainted argument gives a tainted result. `writeLine` does not accept it.
Ledger::writeLine(Ledger::echoString($input));
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
